-- חוק שכר מינימום, התשמ"ז-1987 — sections 1, 2, 3 and 11: what the minimum
-- wage is, that an employee of 18 is owed at least it (in proportion to his
-- position and the time he worked), which components of his pay count
-- toward it, and that the law adds to what an agreement, an arrangement or
-- a contract gives and never takes from it. The text is
-- laws/minimum-wage-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים
-- הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: the corpus's agreements and circulars speak of "השלמת
-- השכר עד לשכר המינימום כמשמעותו בחוק" — the top-up an employer pays where
-- the pay that counts falls short of the minimum — and say which of their
-- supplements and grants are left out of it. Leaving a component out of
-- the pay that counts makes the top-up larger, so an instrument that does
-- so adds to the law (§11); an instrument whose top-up came to less than
-- the law's would be below its floor, and the root's precedence
-- (l4/lib/precedence.l4) lets the floor govern.
--
-- The amount itself is not in these sections: §1 defines it as a share of
-- the average wage "as increased under this law", the Minister publishes
-- it by notice (§6), and temporary provisions have raised it. So the
-- monthly minimum wage is an input of every rule here, never a number.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT vocabulary

§ `חוק שכר מינימום — הרצפה`

`why the Minimum Wage Law's sections state no amount` MEANS
    `set elsewhere` "שר העבודה, בהודעה ברשומות לפי סעיף 6 לחוק שכר מינימום, וחוקי הוראת השעה שמעלים את סכומי שכר המינימום"

§§ `1`

-- "השכר הממוצע" is as section 1 of the National Insurance Law defines it
-- (the National Insurance Institute publishes it). The monthly minimum
-- wage is 47.5% of it as it stands on 1 April of each year, and as
-- increased under the law: the share is the floor of the definition, the
-- amount as increased is the published one (an input). The daily minimum
-- is the 25th part of the monthly for a six-day week and the 21⅔th part
-- for a five-day week; the hourly the 186th part.
@ref law:1
`the Minimum Wage Law's share of the average wage` MEANS 47.5%

GIVEN `the average wage on 1 April` IS A NUMBER @desc as section 1 of the National Insurance Law defines it, published by the National Insurance Institute
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly minimum wage by the definition's share` `the average wage on 1 April` IS
    `the average wage on 1 April` TIMES `the Minimum Wage Law's share of the average wage`

DECLARE `working week under the Minimum Wage Law` IS ONE OF
    `a six-day week under the Minimum Wage Law`
    `a five-day week under the Minimum Wage Law`

GIVEN `the monthly minimum wage` IS A NUMBER @desc as the Minister publishes it under section 6; an input
      w IS A `working week under the Minimum Wage Law`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the daily minimum wage under the Minimum Wage Law` `the monthly minimum wage` w IS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `a six-day week under the Minimum Wage Law` THEN `the monthly minimum wage` DIVIDED BY 25
    WHEN `a five-day week under the Minimum Wage Law` THEN `the monthly minimum wage` DIVIDED BY (21 PLUS 2 DIVIDED BY 3)

GIVEN `the monthly minimum wage` IS A NUMBER @desc as the Minister publishes it under section 6; an input
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hourly minimum wage under the Minimum Wage Law` `the monthly minimum wage` IS
    `the monthly minimum wage` DIVIDED BY 186

#ASSERT `the daily minimum wage under the Minimum Wage Law` 5000 `a six-day week under the Minimum Wage Law` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the daily minimum wage under the Minimum Wage Law` 6500 `a five-day week under the Minimum Wage Law` EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the hourly minimum wage under the Minimum Wage Law` 5580 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the monthly minimum wage by the definition's share` 10000 EQUALS 4750

§§ `2`

-- (א): an employee who has turned 18, in a full position as customary at
-- his workplace, is owed by his employer pay no less than the monthly,
-- daily or hourly minimum, as the case may be. (ב): in a part position, a
-- minimum in proportion to it. (ג): absent from work, his minimum shrinks
-- in proportion to the time absent — and where he is paid for the absence
-- under a law, a contract, a collective agreement, an extension order or
-- another collective arrangement, or a provident fund's binding rules,
-- that payment follows the arrangement, not this section. So the floor is
-- on the time he worked; what he is paid for an absence is the
-- arrangement's.
@ref law:2
GIVEN `the employee's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 2 of the Minimum Wage Law reaches the employee` `the employee's age` IF
    `the employee's age` AT LEAST 18

GIVEN `the monthly minimum wage` IS A NUMBER @desc as the Minister publishes it under section 6; an input
      `the share of a full position` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for a full position as customary at the workplace
      `the share of the time absent` IS A NUMBER @desc the part of the month's working time he was absent, paid or not; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the minimum wage owed for the month under section 2` `the monthly minimum wage` `the share of a full position` `the share of the time absent` IS
    `the monthly minimum wage` TIMES `the share of a full position` TIMES (1 MINUS `the share of the time absent`)

-- What the employer must add where the pay that counts (§3) falls short
-- of the minimum owed: the top-up, "השלמת השכר עד לשכר המינימום".
GIVEN `the minimum wage owed` IS A NUMBER, `the pay that counts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the top-up the Minimum Wage Law requires` `the minimum wage owed` `the pay that counts` IS
    max 0 (`the minimum wage owed` MINUS `the pay that counts`)

#ASSERT NOT `section 2 of the Minimum Wage Law reaches the employee` 17
#ASSERT `the minimum wage owed for the month under section 2` 6000 0.5 0 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `the minimum wage owed for the month under section 2` 6000 1 0.25 EQUALS 4500
#ASSERT `the top-up the Minimum Wage Law requires` 5300 4354.23 EQUALS 945.77
#ASSERT `the top-up the Minimum Wage Law requires` 5300 6000 EQUALS 0

§§ `3`

-- (א): the pay that counts toward §2 is what the employer pays for a
-- regular working day as customary at the workplace. (ב): counted are
-- (1) the basic or the combined salary, (2) a cost-of-living supplement
-- not included in the combined salary, (3) a fixed supplement paid to the
-- employee for his work ((4) and (5) have lapsed); not counted are a
-- family supplement, a seniority supplement, a shift supplement, a
-- premium (measured, agreed, fixed or group), a thirteenth salary, grants
-- on a yearly basis and reimbursements of expenses (meals, subsistence and
-- travel among them). (ג) was repealed; (ה) and (ו) have lapsed.
@ref law:3
DECLARE `pay component under the Minimum Wage Law` IS ONE OF
    `the basic or combined salary, under section 3(ב)(1)`
    `a cost-of-living supplement outside the combined salary, under section 3(ב)(2)`
    `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)`
    `a family supplement, which section 3(ב) leaves out`
    `a seniority supplement, which section 3(ב) leaves out`
    `a shift supplement, which section 3(ב) leaves out`
    `a premium, which section 3(ב) leaves out`
    `a thirteenth salary, which section 3(ב) leaves out`
    `a grant on a yearly basis, which section 3(ב) leaves out`
    `a reimbursement of expenses, which section 3(ב) leaves out`

GIVEN k IS A `pay component under the Minimum Wage Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts toward the minimum wage under section 3` k IF
        k EQUALS `the basic or combined salary, under section 3(ב)(1)`
    OR k EQUALS `a cost-of-living supplement outside the combined salary, under section 3(ב)(2)`
    OR k EQUALS `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)`

@desc One component of a month's pay, as section 3 tells components apart, and what it pays.
DECLARE `component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` HAS
    `its kind under section 3` IS A `pay component under the Minimum Wage Law`
    `its amount in the month`  IS A NUMBER

GIVEN paid IS A LIST OF `component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pay that counts under section 3` paid IS
    sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD IF `counts toward the minimum wage under section 3` (p's `its kind under section 3`)
                            THEN p's `its amount in the month`
                            ELSE 0) paid)

-- (ד): an employee not paid by the components of (ב)(1) and (2), or by
-- part of them, has his regular pay without supplements counted instead;
-- that is the amount a caller gives as the basic salary.

`a month of combined salary, a fixed supplement, seniority and travel` MEANS
    LIST `component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `the basic or combined salary, under section 3(ב)(1)` 4000,
         `component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300,
         `component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a seniority supplement, which section 3(ב) leaves out` 500,
         `component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a reimbursement of expenses, which section 3(ב) leaves out` 200

#ASSERT `the pay that counts under section 3` `a month of combined salary, a fixed supplement, seniority and travel` EQUALS 4300
#ASSERT NOT `counts toward the minimum wage under section 3` `a grant on a yearly basis, which section 3(ב) leaves out`

§§ `11`

-- The law, save §§9 and 10, adds to an employee's right under a law, a
-- collective agreement, a collective arrangement or a contract of
-- employment, and does not take from it: of what the law gives and what
-- another source gives for the same right, the employee has the larger.
-- (§§9 and 10 — no claim to raise pay above the minimum because the
-- minimum was set or updated, and the average wage computed without the
-- minimum's changes — are not pinned.)
@ref law:11
GIVEN `what the Minimum Wage Law gives` IS A NUMBER, `what another source gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what governs between the Minimum Wage Law and another source` `what the Minimum Wage Law gives` `what another source gives` IS
    max `what the Minimum Wage Law gives` `what another source gives`

-- An instrument's own top-up — leaving some of its supplements out of the
-- pay that counts, say — falls below the law's floor only if it comes to
-- less than the top-up the law requires.
GIVEN `the top-up the instrument gives` IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum wage owed` IS A NUMBER
      `the pay that counts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument's top-up falls below the Minimum Wage Law` `the top-up the instrument gives` `the minimum wage owed` `the pay that counts` IF
    `the top-up the instrument gives` LESS THAN `the top-up the Minimum Wage Law requires` `the minimum wage owed` `the pay that counts`

#ASSERT `what governs between the Minimum Wage Law and another source` 5300 5000 EQUALS 5300
#ASSERT `what governs between the Minimum Wage Law and another source` 5300 5500 EQUALS 5500
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument's top-up falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 945.77 5300 4548.26
#ASSERT `the instrument's top-up falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 700 5300 4548.26
